                        "form": "die Parenthesen"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "933bf5be-f9e9-39ca-b09f-cbb2ae47706d",
                        "entry_id": "985714bb-423e-374a-931a-ab61122df604",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Einschub in einen Satz, der mit diesem Satz keine grammatische Verbindung hat"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "special"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c6b58450-aaa3-4a13-a1ec-5b2050fc9076",
                                "sense_id": "933bf5be-f9e9-39ca-b09f-cbb2ae47706d",
                                "text": "In dem Satz „Morgen wird es – so behaupte ich jetzt einfach mal – endlich wieder schönes Wetter geben“ ist das Syntagma „so behaupte ich jetzt einfach mal“ eine Parenthese."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "221b5a74-4659-47bd-b26c-fb4d255e157a",
                                "sense_id": "933bf5be-f9e9-39ca-b09f-cbb2ae47706d",
                                "text": "In dem Satz „Und dann, meine Damen und Herren, können wir endlich zum Ende kommen“ ist die Anrede „meine Damen und Herren“ eine Parenthese."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "70a6ae77-208b-42c2-a1ca-0c69c54612f1",
                                "sense_id": "933bf5be-f9e9-39ca-b09f-cbb2ae47706d",
                                "text": "„Eine besondere Art zusammengesetzter Satz liegt vor, wenn ein syntaktisch eigenständiger Satz in einen anderen Satz eingeschoben oder ‚eingeschaltet‘ wird (…). Der eingeschobene Satz wird dann als Parenthese oder Schaltsatz bezeichnet.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "67368a16-e0dd-4950-b954-351a13c72e18",
                                "sense_id": "933bf5be-f9e9-39ca-b09f-cbb2ae47706d",
                                "text": "„In der Stilkritik geht es vielfach um einen zu vermeidenden Substantivstil, den als ausufernd betrachteten Umgang mit Adjektiven, Schachtelsätze oder als negativ stigmatisierte Satzunterbrechungen durch Parenthesen (…).“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a01f4bf6-74f0-310f-a2b2-81e4d3b9c392",
                        "entry_id": "985714bb-423e-374a-931a-ab61122df604",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Satzzeichen (Gedankenstriche, Klammern oder Kommas), mit denen ein Einschub in den Satz markiert wird"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "special"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "efd4c202-f109-4d03-8f8f-ca22ac64d741",
                                "sense_id": "a01f4bf6-74f0-310f-a2b2-81e4d3b9c392",
                                "text": "„Es gibt noch ein zweites Satzzeichen, um ein Satzgefüge durchsichtig zu machen: die Parenthese (Schaltzeichen), das heißt Gedankenstriche ( — ) vor und hinter einer Einschaltung.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d7e5f6ca-b6b6-49ab-b633-ae98fe0a4e56",
                                "sense_id": "a01f4bf6-74f0-310f-a2b2-81e4d3b9c392",
                                "text": "„Das Zeichen E. bedeutet ‚Eigenthümer‘; wohnt derselbe nicht in dem Hause, so ist seine Wohnung in Parenthese beigefügt.\""
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "05ba136d-f6cc-4b73-bbae-b052bdab27fd",
                        "source_entry_id": "985714bb-423e-374a-931a-ab61122df604",
                        "source_sense_id": "933bf5be-f9e9-39ca-b09f-cbb2ae47706d",
                        "target_lang_word": "parenthesis",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "parenthesis",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "97e19b41-fd12-38b3-854c-18e7061f54e1",
                                        "entry_id": "51d8ab5f-448d-3d45-ab21-48ca146d6d60",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A clause, phrase or word which is inserted (usually for explanation or amplification) into a passage which is already grammatically complete, and usually marked off with brackets, commas or dashes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5ba475e1-585b-4c18-897d-49478e8c5a20",
                                                "sense_id": "97e19b41-fd12-38b3-854c-18e7061f54e1",
                                                "text": "How expressive this little parenthesis: \"Sakuntalâ makes a chiding gesture with her finger\"!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "06e51e09-b8bb-3137-aec8-2e3cdfbfdb96",
                                        "entry_id": "51d8ab5f-448d-3d45-ab21-48ca146d6d60",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Either of a pair of brackets, especially (mainly US) round brackets, ( and ) (used to enclose parenthetical material in a text)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fdd4952b-44d1-49c7-a626-6dab39384da6",
                                                "sense_id": "06e51e09-b8bb-3137-aec8-2e3cdfbfdb96",
                                                "text": "There be five manner of points and divisions most used among cunning men; the which if they be well used, make the sentence very light and easy to be understood, both to the reader and hearer: and they be these, virgil,—come,—parenthesis,—plain point,—interrogative[…] it is a slender stroke leaning forward, betokening a little short rest, without any perfectness yet of sentence."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4be00a79-ca18-4e99-80be-d9b6c9a16d59",
                                                "sense_id": "06e51e09-b8bb-3137-aec8-2e3cdfbfdb96",
                                                "text": "Whoever introduced the several points, it seems that a full-point, a point called come, answering to our colon-point, a point called virgil answering to our comma-point, the parenthesis-points and interrogative-point, were used at the close of the fourteenth, or beginning of the fifteenth century."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f9ee30f2-5657-4025-958f-fb7e679b5eea",
                                                "sense_id": "06e51e09-b8bb-3137-aec8-2e3cdfbfdb96",
                                                "text": "[T]he present research also made an effort to approach a greater accuracy in presenting the original sources of borrowed words. This was achieved by presenting etymons from Hindustani in the Devanagari script followed by a transliteration in the Roman alphabet in parentheses."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2842b188-8020-3a4e-9680-5736958a21d8",
                                        "entry_id": "51d8ab5f-448d-3d45-ab21-48ca146d6d60",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A digression; the use of such digressions."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "rhetoric",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c923facb-901f-46af-95bd-3839c7678266",
                                                "sense_id": "2842b188-8020-3a4e-9680-5736958a21d8",
                                                "text": "Mr. Trevanion was one of those talkers, who are too much engrossed with their own subject matter to have much attention to bestow elsewhere; with them silence is attention. Ethel's wandering eye, and lip, tremulous with its effort to speak, would never have attracted his notice. To his utter astonishment, she interrupted a parenthesis, as brilliant as the rocket which it depicted, by saying,—\n\"Mr. Trevanion, I do not know what you will think of my boldness, but I must speak to you.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b09b7d4b-84fd-40a5-b78b-e31ba263cff0",
                                                "sense_id": "2842b188-8020-3a4e-9680-5736958a21d8",
                                                "text": "Ryan Bingham (George Clooney): I thought I was a part of your life.\nAlex Goran (Vera Farmiga): I thought we signed up for the same thing[…] I thought our relationship was perfectly clear. You are an escape. You're a break from our normal lives. You're a parenthesis.\nRyan Bingham (George Clooney): I'm a parenthesis?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "275a4f28-4828-3164-b7ca-e327b3d735cf",
                                        "entry_id": "51d8ab5f-448d-3d45-ab21-48ca146d6d60",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Such brackets as used to clarify expressions by grouping those terms affected by a common operator, or to enclose the components of a vector or the elements of a matrix."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "77bea9f0-ce4b-4794-bca7-9bef90e08fbd",
                        "source_entry_id": "985714bb-423e-374a-931a-ab61122df604",
                        "source_sense_id": "933bf5be-f9e9-39ca-b09f-cbb2ae47706d",
